1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,700
(EP06 Behind-the-Scenes)

2
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:05,980
(Behind-the-Scenes 1)

3
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:08,020
(Special surprise for our top CP fans)

4
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:12,830
(Making familiar bracelets)
This feels familiar.

5
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:13,580
Have a seat.

6
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:15,980
(Pulls out a chair)

7
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:20,740
(Glances)

8
00:00:26,030 --> 00:00:27,460
(A little treat for everyone)
Bonus Segment.

9
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:27,870
Yeah.

10
00:00:27,870 --> 00:00:29,230
Let's say hi to everyone first.

11
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:31,590
Hello, everyone.

12
00:00:31,590 --> 00:00:33,070
(Cui Kaiyi)
I'm Cui Kaiyi.

13
00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:34,230
(Cao Yiheng)
I'm Cao Yiheng.

14
00:00:34,230 --> 00:00:36,110
First of all, thank you so much

15
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:37,420
for all your love and support.

16
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:38,540
Thank you, everyone.

17
00:00:39,550 --> 00:00:41,180
So today, we've also prepared

18
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:43,180
(Some surprises and gifts for everyone)
a few surprises and gifts.

19
00:00:43,180 --> 00:00:44,550
They're things we normally use,

20
00:00:44,550 --> 00:00:45,750
the same ones everyone has in the house.

21
00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:46,950
(Matching tumbler)
The tumbler.

22
00:00:46,950 --> 00:00:48,070
(Matching heart-shaped cushion)
The sofa cushion.

23
00:00:48,070 --> 00:00:49,470
(Matching canvas bag)
And the canvas bag.

24
00:00:49,470 --> 00:00:51,110
The one I carried when you
took me to the school.

25
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:52,980
That canvas bag.
Yeah.

26
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:53,790
And besides those,

27
00:00:53,790 --> 00:00:55,270
we've also prepared

28
00:00:55,270 --> 00:00:56,220
some extra special gifts.

29
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:57,300
So some lucky friends

30
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,380
will get something special,

31
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:00,660
a little something extra.

32
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:04,350
They're all right here.

33
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:05,830
(Today's mission: Make bracelets)
We'll make them ourselves.

34
00:01:06,190 --> 00:01:07,110
Let's start making them.

35
00:01:08,870 --> 00:01:09,590
They're so pretty.

36
00:01:10,270 --> 00:01:11,150
There are so many colors.

37
00:01:11,870 --> 00:01:13,220
You're better at this.

38
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:14,910
And bracelets

39
00:01:14,910 --> 00:01:16,980
(Holds special memories)
mean a lot to us too.

40
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:18,710
We kept wearing ours afterward.

41
00:01:20,790 --> 00:01:22,950
Why do you like bracelets?

42
00:01:22,950 --> 00:01:24,180
Because I feel like

43
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:25,940
you can keep them for a long time.

44
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:27,300
You can always take them out
and look at them,

45
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:28,230
or just keep wearing them.

46
00:01:28,230 --> 00:01:29,910
Whenever you see one, it reminds you of us

47
00:01:29,910 --> 00:01:32,700
and the time we spent making them.

48
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:33,190
Yeah.

49
00:01:36,550 --> 00:01:38,100
Let's get started.

50
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:38,900
(Getting ready to make bracelets)
Okay.

51
00:01:39,190 --> 00:01:40,220
You make one for a guy,

52
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:41,420
and I'll make one for a girl.

53
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:42,580
My wrist is 16 centimeters.

54
00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:43,700
You can use the 15-centimeter one.

55
00:01:43,910 --> 00:01:44,830
See, 16 is actually

56
00:01:44,830 --> 00:01:45,550
already pretty big.

57
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:46,820
(Comparing sizes)

58
00:01:47,060 --> 00:01:48,180
Sixteen and seventeen.

59
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:49,180
Okay, sixteen and seventeen.

60
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:49,860
Yeah.

61
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:51,630
Let's start with purple.

62
00:01:52,510 --> 00:01:53,470
Look at this one.

63
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:55,580
Pretty.

64
00:01:55,580 --> 00:01:56,510
Fasten it like this.

65
00:01:56,710 --> 00:01:58,510
We should make a few special ones.

66
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:00,260
Okay.

67
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:00,980
(Special editions coming up)

68
00:02:02,030 --> 00:02:03,310
I'll make this one.

69
00:02:04,350 --> 00:02:06,070
I'll put my heart into it.

70
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:10,660
Sixteen and seventeen.
Think that'll work?

71
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:11,460
No problem.

72
00:02:12,910 --> 00:02:14,310
I'm just worried it might be too small.

73
00:02:14,310 --> 00:02:15,260
If it's too big,

74
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:16,300
whoever gets it

75
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:17,060
can always take some beads off.

76
00:02:17,060 --> 00:02:19,180
But if it's too small,
they can't add any.

77
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:19,820
(Thoughtful)

78
00:02:20,550 --> 00:02:22,140
Perfect, I'm done with this part.

79
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:22,940
Same here.

80
00:02:24,870 --> 00:02:25,580
Let's string the beads.

81
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:28,180
But I need another needle.

82
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:29,380
Mine's too bent.

83
00:02:29,380 --> 00:02:30,190
Have you thought of

84
00:02:30,190 --> 00:02:31,460
a design for the girls' one?

85
00:02:31,460 --> 00:02:32,020
(Glances)

86
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,380
I need to string mine first,

87
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:33,700
babe.

88
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:35,260
I need to string mine first,

89
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:36,300
babe.

90
00:02:45,310 --> 00:02:46,470
(Glances)
You're so fast.

91
00:02:47,630 --> 00:02:48,910
I'm good at this.

92
00:02:58,230 --> 00:02:59,350
What do I do next?

93
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:00,550
I'll do it.

94
00:03:00,550 --> 00:03:01,660
(Leave it to me)

95
00:03:01,910 --> 00:03:03,790
Then push this over here.

96
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:08,060
(Moves closer)

97
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:08,860
Look.

98
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:11,670
Then do this.

99
00:03:11,910 --> 00:03:13,430
Bring this end through.

100
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:15,430
I think I remember now.

101
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:18,100
Nice.

102
00:03:18,910 --> 00:03:20,750
I think I'm better at stringing beads.

103
00:03:21,870 --> 00:03:22,500
I'll do the stringing.

104
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:23,870
Yeah, you keep stringing them.

105
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:27,780
(Glances)

106
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:28,980
Got it.

107
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:31,460
Nice.

108
00:03:32,430 --> 00:03:33,630
I did it.

109
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:35,620
(Smiles)

110
00:03:39,190 --> 00:03:40,540
Okay, I'm done stringing mine.

111
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:41,300
Nice.

112
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:42,310
I did it.

113
00:03:44,110 --> 00:03:45,340
Done.

114
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:48,950
(Shows it from every angle)
Done.

115
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:52,460
Done.

116
00:03:52,820 --> 00:03:53,860
One down.

117
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:54,820
(First amethyst bracelet complete)

118
00:03:55,870 --> 00:03:56,870
For the next one,

119
00:03:57,180 --> 00:03:57,660
I think red.

120
00:03:57,660 --> 00:03:58,390
Let's do red first.

121
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:04,340
(Thinking)

122
00:04:05,790 --> 00:04:07,950
I'm thinking of making one

123
00:04:07,950 --> 00:04:09,110
that's truly one of a kind.

124
00:04:09,870 --> 00:04:10,750
Whoever gets this one

125
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:12,390
will be the luckiest person ever.

126
00:04:12,670 --> 00:04:13,790
(Designing a special one)
The luckiest?

127
00:04:15,950 --> 00:04:17,150
(Yiheng's special design)
Yellow and green.

128
00:04:17,470 --> 00:04:21,310
Aren't those our signature colors?

129
00:04:22,830 --> 00:04:23,510
What do you think?

130
00:04:23,670 --> 00:04:24,540
Our signature colors.

131
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:25,150
Nice.

132
00:04:25,150 --> 00:04:26,910
(Another special one
in our signature colors)

133
00:04:26,910 --> 00:04:28,750
Make a purple one to go with it.

134
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:29,940
Sure.

135
00:04:30,310 --> 00:04:30,710
Okay.

136
00:04:30,710 --> 00:04:31,870
I've finished two more.

137
00:04:31,870 --> 00:04:33,390
I think I'm getting better at this.

138
00:04:33,390 --> 00:04:34,670
Does mine look good?

139
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:35,580
(Looks right away)

140
00:04:37,070 --> 00:04:37,990
(Kaiyi's mixed-color design)
Pretty good.

141
00:04:37,990 --> 00:04:39,190
I think the white beads

142
00:04:39,190 --> 00:04:40,550
look better mixed in.

143
00:04:40,550 --> 00:04:42,270
I'm calling this one "Snake."

144
00:04:42,470 --> 00:04:43,750
It's inspired by the Snake game.

145
00:04:44,310 --> 00:04:46,150
(Another irregular "Snake" bracelet)
Why are the beads different sizes?

146
00:04:46,710 --> 00:04:47,830
It's a gradual pattern.

147
00:04:47,910 --> 00:04:49,590
They get bigger as they go.

148
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:51,070
Try this one on.

149
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:53,900
(Another blue-and-white bracelet)
It makes your skin look brighter.

150
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:54,620
Not bad.

151
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:55,430
It really does.

152
00:04:55,830 --> 00:04:57,190
Whoever gets this one

153
00:04:57,190 --> 00:04:58,350
is even luckier than the last person.

154
00:04:58,590 --> 00:04:59,230
(Double the luck)
Okay.

155
00:04:59,230 --> 00:05:00,620
Mine are the regular ones.

156
00:05:00,620 --> 00:05:02,630
Yours are the special ones.

157
00:05:02,630 --> 00:05:03,940
(Another extra-lucky special bracelet)

158
00:05:03,940 --> 00:05:05,620
I'll leave the stringing to you.

159
00:05:05,620 --> 00:05:06,420
(Dividing up the work)
Okay.

160
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:09,020
(Matching the colors)

161
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:10,700
(Stringing the beads)

162
00:05:11,910 --> 00:05:14,340
I feel like I could open a shop soon.

163
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:15,860
Everlasting YiHeng

164
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:16,910
Bracelet Shop.

165
00:05:16,940 --> 00:05:18,580
(Smiles)

166
00:05:20,350 --> 00:05:21,350
Done in no time.

167
00:05:25,460 --> 00:05:26,020
Okay.

168
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:27,070
This one's done too.

169
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:34,620
Okay.

170
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:35,550
Finally, we're done stringing them.

171
00:05:35,550 --> 00:05:36,270
All done.

172
00:05:36,270 --> 00:05:37,830
Let's count all 30 again.

173
00:05:37,990 --> 00:05:38,820
Two, four, six.

174
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:40,230
Eight, ten, twelve, fourteen.

175
00:05:40,230 --> 00:05:41,950
Sixteen, eighteen, twenty, twenty-two.

176
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:43,180
Twenty-four.

177
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:44,020
Twenty-six.

178
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:45,460
Twenty-eight.

179
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:46,740
Thirty.

180
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:47,900
(15 pairs of bracelets complete)
Okay.

181
00:05:48,230 --> 00:05:50,110
We've prepared three games.

182
00:05:50,110 --> 00:05:52,190
Every time we complete one,

183
00:05:52,190 --> 00:05:53,270
we'll unlock some gifts.

184
00:05:53,790 --> 00:05:55,350
Why don't we play the games first?

185
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:56,200
(Yiheng and Kaiyi's
Two Truths and a Lie)

186
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:56,860
(They each share three things
about themselves)

187
00:05:56,860 --> 00:05:57,320
(Two are true, one is a lie)

188
00:05:57,320 --> 00:05:58,040
(Guess correctly to give away
five pairs of bracelets)

189
00:05:58,190 --> 00:05:58,700
Let me think.

190
00:05:58,700 --> 00:05:59,550
I need three.

191
00:06:00,830 --> 00:06:02,830
On our

192
00:06:03,630 --> 00:06:04,820
first date,

193
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:06,790
I actually wasn't that scared

194
00:06:07,350 --> 00:06:08,620
(Two Truths and a Lie:)
of the high-altitude activity.

195
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:10,180
(1. I wasn't scared of heights)
Second,

196
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:11,830
when we were in the study,

197
00:06:11,830 --> 00:06:13,350
you drew that little bunny.

198
00:06:13,350 --> 00:06:15,630
I honestly thought you just really liked

199
00:06:15,630 --> 00:06:18,110
(2. I thought you liked the bunny)
the bunny in the study.

200
00:06:18,110 --> 00:06:20,430
And third,

201
00:06:20,430 --> 00:06:22,660
(3. You look good in glasses)
you look good in glasses.

202
00:06:23,900 --> 00:06:26,110
You look good in glasses.

203
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:29,820
I only need one fake one.

204
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:30,630
Right.

205
00:06:31,350 --> 00:06:32,620
I'll guess,

206
00:06:32,620 --> 00:06:33,740
(Yiheng's guess)
the first one.

207
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:34,590
(Her fear of heights is the lie)
Why?

208
00:06:34,590 --> 00:06:36,710
(Remembers)
You've said you're afraid of heights.

209
00:06:39,750 --> 00:06:40,620
Your turn.

210
00:06:42,070 --> 00:06:43,420
First,

211
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:45,660
I was waiting for you for ages
when we first arrived at the house.

212
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:47,040
(Answers instantly)
True.

213
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,040
(Two Truths and a Lie:
1. I waited for you on day one)

214
00:06:49,790 --> 00:06:53,140
Then I've only cooked for you once.

215
00:06:53,140 --> 00:06:53,700
(2. I've only cooked for you once)

216
00:06:53,710 --> 00:06:55,950
(3. Eyes were on you during the dinner)
I kept watching you during the dinner.

217
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:57,700
(Already knows)

218
00:06:57,710 --> 00:06:59,070
The cooking one has to be the lie.

219
00:06:59,070 --> 00:07:01,350
(Kaiyi's guess: The cooking is a lie)
You've cooked for me several times.

220
00:07:02,270 --> 00:07:03,710
What did you make?

221
00:07:03,710 --> 00:07:04,700
Eight Treasure tofu.

222
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:06,070
And stir-fried squid tentacles.

223
00:07:06,070 --> 00:07:07,230
Right, the squid.

224
00:07:07,230 --> 00:07:10,230
(Garlic butter shrimp)
And the garlic butter shrimp.

225
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:12,270
(Luosifen, stewed pear soup)
Luosifen and stewed pear soup.

226
00:07:12,270 --> 00:07:13,220
Eggs with green peppers.

227
00:07:13,220 --> 00:07:14,180
Spicy fried eggs.

228
00:07:14,180 --> 00:07:15,510
Yeah, so many.

229
00:07:15,510 --> 00:07:17,070
You've made loads of things.

230
00:07:17,070 --> 00:07:19,380
So we cleared the first game.

231
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:21,100
(Unlocked ten bracelets)
That's ten unlocked.

232
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:21,760
(Yiheng and Kaiyi's Witch's Poison)

233
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:22,280
(Each chooses one bead as their poison.)

234
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:22,800
(Use any method
to get clues about the other's poison.)

235
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:23,440
(First to identify the other's poison
wins and gets to choose a punishment.)

236
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:24,140
(Complete the game
to give away ten pairs of bracelets.)

237
00:07:24,140 --> 00:07:25,420
(Choosing the poison)

238
00:07:26,940 --> 00:07:27,860
(Kaiyi's poison: Dark purple bead)

239
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:28,660
Okay.

240
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:33,220
(Moves closer)

241
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:36,700
(Snickers)

242
00:07:37,230 --> 00:07:38,870
Let's see if I can tell by the sound.

243
00:07:40,340 --> 00:07:41,620
(Yiheng's poison: Dark green bead)

244
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:44,580
(Sets it down gently)

245
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:46,700
(Still trying to locate it by sound)
Done.

246
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:49,140
(Glances)

247
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:50,420
Why was that so quiet?

248
00:07:52,470 --> 00:07:53,550
What are you laughing at?

249
00:07:53,790 --> 00:07:54,580
Nothing.

250
00:07:54,580 --> 00:07:55,780
(Can't hold it in)

251
00:07:56,830 --> 00:07:57,910
You guess first.

252
00:07:59,460 --> 00:08:00,980
(Kaiyi's poison, Yiheng's poison)

253
00:08:01,590 --> 00:08:03,070
Would you call it a dark color?

254
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:04,220
Yeah.

255
00:08:05,830 --> 00:08:09,630
Is the bead smaller than average?

256
00:08:10,550 --> 00:08:11,630
Smaller than average.

257
00:08:11,630 --> 00:08:12,110
Average.

258
00:08:12,390 --> 00:08:13,100
Okay.

259
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:14,500
Is yours purple?

260
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:15,300
Yes.

261
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:16,940
(Narrowing it down)

262
00:08:17,430 --> 00:08:18,950
Is it a light shade?

263
00:08:19,670 --> 00:08:20,590
No.

264
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:23,500
I'm guessing this one.

265
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:24,110
This one.

266
00:08:26,390 --> 00:08:27,070
This one.

267
00:08:27,750 --> 00:08:28,550
(Gets it right first try)
Yes.

268
00:08:29,750 --> 00:08:30,670
You lose.

269
00:08:30,670 --> 00:08:31,790
You pick the punishment.

270
00:08:31,990 --> 00:08:33,670
Sing us a song.

271
00:08:33,670 --> 00:08:34,340
(Excited)

272
00:08:35,470 --> 00:08:36,190
Sing a song.

273
00:08:38,580 --> 00:08:39,860
(Looking at each other)

274
00:08:42,510 --> 00:08:43,500
You sing really well.

275
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:44,390
Just sing a couple of lines.

276
00:08:46,510 --> 00:08:47,870
♪Not yet♪

277
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:52,290
♪Have I cooked red beans for you♪

278
00:08:52,610 --> 00:08:55,810
♪Until they became an aching wound♪

279
00:08:56,070 --> 00:08:59,320
♪Maybe from now on♪

280
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:04,150
♪I'll learn to cherish
a love that lasts♪

281
00:09:04,310 --> 00:09:08,150
♪When we've seen all there is to see♪

282
00:09:08,390 --> 00:09:10,980
♪Maybe you'll stay with me♪

283
00:09:10,980 --> 00:09:14,150
♪And watch the years gently pass♪

284
00:09:23,430 --> 00:09:24,660
That's another one unlocked.

285
00:09:24,660 --> 00:09:25,380
(Unlocked 10 pairs)
You're amazing.

286
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:26,100
So amazing.

287
00:09:28,310 --> 00:09:29,670
Now for our last game.

288
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:30,700
(Yiheng and Kaiyi's
Try Not to Laugh Challenge)

289
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:31,340
(Open your eyes
and look at each other.)

290
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:32,060
(Make the other person laugh
any way you can.)

291
00:09:32,060 --> 00:09:32,680
(First to make the other laugh wins.)

292
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:33,520
(Complete the game
to give away a Heart Signal Polaroid.)

293
00:09:33,780 --> 00:09:34,980
Three.

294
00:09:34,980 --> 00:09:35,740
Two.

295
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:36,180
One.

296
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:36,740
Open your eyes.

297
00:09:37,020 --> 00:09:39,340
(Looking at each other)

298
00:09:39,420 --> 00:09:41,020
(Holding back a laugh)

299
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:43,340
(Holds it in)

300
00:09:45,700 --> 00:09:46,860
(Leans closer)

301
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:50,620
(Stares)

302
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:02,460
(Compliment attack)
Your side profile looks really good.

303
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:03,910
Your side profile looks really good.

304
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:07,780
(Secretly pleased)

305
00:10:08,510 --> 00:10:09,750
Don't you feel like laughing?

306
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:11,500
Not really.

307
00:10:12,860 --> 00:10:14,580
(Holds it in)

308
00:10:22,820 --> 00:10:23,900
(Can't hold it in)
What's wrong with you?

309
00:10:24,710 --> 00:10:26,540
What's wrong?

310
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:27,700
I didn't even do anything.

311
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:30,460
Can I ask

312
00:10:30,460 --> 00:10:31,310
what was so funny?

313
00:10:31,310 --> 00:10:32,980
Does my face look funny to you?

314
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:33,860
(Holds her hand)
No.

315
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:34,950
What was it?

316
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:37,820
(Thinking of what to say)

317
00:10:39,270 --> 00:10:40,430
What was so funny?

318
00:10:40,990 --> 00:10:42,190
You're just too cute.

319
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:44,660
(Smiles)

320
00:10:45,030 --> 00:10:46,860
So I'm cute, and that's funny?

321
00:10:46,860 --> 00:10:48,300
You did

322
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:49,310
all those moves,

323
00:10:49,310 --> 00:10:50,980
then suddenly you just froze.

324
00:10:52,710 --> 00:10:53,990
You looked so helpless.

325
00:11:01,060 --> 00:11:01,820
Okay.

326
00:11:02,220 --> 00:11:03,500
Even though we lost,

327
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:04,380
we still want

328
00:11:04,380 --> 00:11:04,980
to share

329
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:07,220
these gifts with everyone.

330
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:08,470
We'll each pack half.

331
00:11:08,470 --> 00:11:09,270
Okay.

332
00:11:14,150 --> 00:11:15,790
Here, give me a few more boxes.

333
00:11:15,790 --> 00:11:16,740
(Gets the message)

334
00:11:18,390 --> 00:11:19,110
(Hands them over)
Keep each pair together.

335
00:11:19,670 --> 00:11:20,230
Don't mix them up.

336
00:11:20,230 --> 00:11:21,270
I kept them together.

337
00:11:25,860 --> 00:11:26,780
(Follows)

338
00:11:27,350 --> 00:11:28,700
It's okay, I'll give it to you.

339
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:29,420
(Hands it over)

340
00:11:29,990 --> 00:11:31,500
You took my pink one.

341
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:32,910
(Not taking it)
You're packing that one.

342
00:11:33,380 --> 00:11:34,180
Right.

343
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:37,380
(Writing wishes)

344
00:11:38,020 --> 00:11:39,500
(Glances)

345
00:11:40,150 --> 00:11:41,460
Always be happy.

346
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:42,550
Always be blessed.

347
00:11:42,550 --> 00:11:44,220
(Always be happy, always be blessed)

348
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:46,020
(Glancess again)

349
00:11:47,990 --> 00:11:49,510
Don't copy me.

350
00:11:49,510 --> 00:11:50,580
(Leans closer)

351
00:11:51,350 --> 00:11:52,270
What are you sending?

352
00:11:52,270 --> 00:11:53,620
I'm sending you good luck.

353
00:11:53,620 --> 00:11:54,420
Okay.

354
00:11:54,540 --> 00:11:56,740
(Gets an idea)

355
00:11:59,870 --> 00:12:00,750
Let's see what color is next.

356
00:12:01,750 --> 00:12:03,700
Another light pink one.

357
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:04,870
This pinkish-red one.

358
00:12:05,630 --> 00:12:07,950
(A message from both)
How about we both write on the red ones?

359
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:08,940
Sure.

360
00:12:09,350 --> 00:12:13,670
Wishing you happiness always.

361
00:12:13,670 --> 00:12:14,340
(Wishing you happiness always)

362
00:12:14,990 --> 00:12:16,740
I'll write: "Always be joyful."

363
00:12:16,740 --> 00:12:17,350
Or maybe...

364
00:12:17,350 --> 00:12:18,390
(Wishing you happiness always)
Stay healthy always.

365
00:12:18,390 --> 00:12:18,910
Sure.

366
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:26,780
May your

367
00:12:26,780 --> 00:12:28,300
worries fade away.

368
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:29,620
(May your worries fade away)

369
00:12:29,950 --> 00:12:30,910
And your smile brightens each day.

370
00:12:30,910 --> 00:12:31,470
Sure.

371
00:12:31,470 --> 00:12:32,260
Make it rhyme.

372
00:12:32,470 --> 00:12:33,270
Sounds good.

373
00:12:35,430 --> 00:12:37,830
I'll write, "Be yourself."

374
00:12:37,830 --> 00:12:39,750
Don't worry about what others think.

375
00:12:40,350 --> 00:12:41,990
The brave get to enjoy love first.

376
00:12:41,990 --> 00:12:42,460
Sounds good.

377
00:12:43,030 --> 00:12:43,780
Be yourself.

378
00:12:43,780 --> 00:12:44,950
Be happy every day.

379
00:12:46,220 --> 00:12:46,580
Okay.

380
00:12:47,180 --> 00:12:47,440
Okay.

381
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:48,060
(Eat well and get plenty of sleep)

382
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:48,640
(Hope you find your own sunflower)

383
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:49,460
(Eat fewer snacks
and drink fewer sugary drinks)

384
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:50,080
(Here I come, bringing you good luck)

385
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:50,960
(Believe in yourself.
You're strong enough to handle anything)

386
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:51,900
(Stay beautiful and happy always)

387
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:52,500
Here.

388
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:53,870
(Starting to pack)
Here's a pink one for you.

389
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:01,020
(Won't close)

390
00:13:02,550 --> 00:13:04,310
It's really not my packing skills.

391
00:13:04,310 --> 00:13:05,100
Give it to me.

392
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:07,220
(Helps)

393
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:16,780
(A special surprise package)
Here.

394
00:13:22,550 --> 00:13:24,390
You're so good at tying bows.

395
00:13:24,590 --> 00:13:26,070
Genius.

396
00:13:29,670 --> 00:13:30,470
Okay.

397
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:31,900
Put something underneath.

398
00:13:37,270 --> 00:13:39,670
All our gifts are packed.

399
00:13:39,670 --> 00:13:40,670
All done.

400
00:13:40,910 --> 00:13:42,030
We hope

401
00:13:42,030 --> 00:13:43,190
you'll like the gifts.

402
00:13:43,190 --> 00:13:44,350
And we hope

403
00:13:44,350 --> 00:13:46,390
every day brings you happiness

404
00:13:46,390 --> 00:13:47,510
and everything you wish for.

405
00:13:48,190 --> 00:13:49,950
If you get a gift, you get good luck.

406
00:13:50,220 --> 00:13:51,900
And even if you don't,
good luck is still yours.

407
00:13:52,620 --> 00:13:54,100
Bye!

408
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:55,980
(Wishing everyone happiness always)

409
00:13:56,020 --> 00:14:00,980
(Behind-the-Scenes 2)

410
00:14:01,020 --> 00:14:05,980
(Special surprise for our top CP fans)

411
00:14:06,460 --> 00:14:07,540
Three, two, one. Together.

412
00:14:07,990 --> 00:14:08,860
Or you go first.

413
00:14:09,710 --> 00:14:10,510
Let's do it together.

414
00:14:10,940 --> 00:14:11,620
Okay.

415
00:14:12,790 --> 00:14:13,620
Hello, everyone.

416
00:14:13,910 --> 00:14:14,550
Hello, everyone.

417
00:14:14,550 --> 00:14:15,340
(A beat late)

418
00:14:18,070 --> 00:14:19,820
(One more time)
Hello, everyone.

419
00:14:19,820 --> 00:14:20,750
Thank you for all your support.

420
00:14:20,750 --> 00:14:21,870
It's thanks to you

421
00:14:21,870 --> 00:14:23,390
that we get to do this today

422
00:14:23,390 --> 00:14:25,070
(Sun Bohan & Wu Xingying)
and prepare some gifts for you.

423
00:14:25,070 --> 00:14:27,630
(Lots of little gifts)
We've prepared 80 gifts in total.

424
00:14:27,830 --> 00:14:29,030
Besides the cups

425
00:14:29,030 --> 00:14:30,110
we used in the Signal House,

426
00:14:30,270 --> 00:14:31,110
the little cushions,

427
00:14:31,110 --> 00:14:32,310
we also made

428
00:14:32,310 --> 00:14:34,070
these fridge magnets ourselves,

429
00:14:34,070 --> 00:14:34,990
and these little plates.

430
00:14:35,430 --> 00:14:37,710
We also have a few challenges

431
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:38,310
and games today

432
00:14:38,310 --> 00:14:39,900
to unlock the gifts.

433
00:14:39,900 --> 00:14:41,230
Hope you like them.

434
00:14:41,260 --> 00:14:42,820
(Glances)

435
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:47,350
Actually, while preparing

436
00:14:47,350 --> 00:14:48,190
all these gifts,

437
00:14:48,190 --> 00:14:48,790
I think we were even happier

438
00:14:48,790 --> 00:14:50,230
than you'll be receiving them.

439
00:14:50,230 --> 00:14:50,580
Yeah.

440
00:14:50,910 --> 00:14:52,590
Have you ever made pottery before?

441
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:53,780
No.

442
00:14:53,780 --> 00:14:54,340
Never.

443
00:14:54,340 --> 00:14:55,020
(Pottery beginner)

444
00:14:55,020 --> 00:14:56,020
Same here.

445
00:14:56,430 --> 00:14:58,190
(Both beginners)
So today,

446
00:14:58,470 --> 00:14:59,190
we're both trying something new.

447
00:14:59,190 --> 00:15:00,750
Yeah, our first time.

448
00:15:01,430 --> 00:15:03,060
(Making pottery together)
We'll be rusty at first.

449
00:15:03,270 --> 00:15:05,230
but I think we'll get the hang of it.

450
00:15:05,910 --> 00:15:06,910
Yeah. These gifts are really just our way

451
00:15:06,910 --> 00:15:08,390
of giving something back to everyone.

452
00:15:08,430 --> 00:15:10,150
I had a lot of fun making them.

453
00:15:10,150 --> 00:15:10,670
Yeah.

454
00:15:10,670 --> 00:15:12,110
Let's get started.

455
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:12,980
(Xing and Bohan's Lyrics Challenge)

456
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:13,480
(They have three seconds)

457
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:14,280
(to take turns singing
or saying lyrics with the given keyword)

458
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:14,680
(Whoever can't think of one)

459
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:15,200
(must act cute
for the other as punishment)

460
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:15,920
(Get three right to unlock 12 pairs
of fridge magnets)

461
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:17,060
(Reading the rules)

462
00:15:17,550 --> 00:15:18,470
I want to change the punishment.

463
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:21,670
I want you to sing a line
from that song.

464
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:23,420
(Testing the waters)

465
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:24,110
Sure.

466
00:15:24,860 --> 00:15:26,020
(Indulges him)

467
00:15:26,020 --> 00:15:26,750
You sure?

468
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:29,420
(Smiles)

469
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:31,270
The first keyword is heart.

470
00:15:31,270 --> 00:15:33,700
(First keyword: Heart)

471
00:15:33,710 --> 00:15:34,750
This is a little embarrassing.

472
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:41,990
♪How can two hearts
so close say goodbye?♪

473
00:15:42,380 --> 00:15:43,460
(Bohan gets one right)

474
00:15:43,460 --> 00:15:44,820
Your turn.

475
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:46,780
(Thinking)

476
00:15:46,990 --> 00:15:48,550
Three seconds. Time's up.

477
00:15:49,310 --> 00:15:50,750
Okay, I lose this round.

478
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:51,700
(Indulges him again)

479
00:15:51,790 --> 00:15:53,350
Sing a line or act cute?

480
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:55,460
(Thinking)

481
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:56,750
I've never heard you sing before.

482
00:15:59,190 --> 00:16:01,750
(Grants his wish)
♪What do I do when it rains?♪

483
00:16:02,310 --> 00:16:03,590
So what do you do?

484
00:16:03,590 --> 00:16:05,310
I'm not singing the next line with you.

485
00:16:05,860 --> 00:16:07,060
(Shy)

486
00:16:07,060 --> 00:16:08,270
Isn't it four words?

487
00:16:10,630 --> 00:16:12,110
(What do I do when it rains?)
I... what was it again?

488
00:16:12,110 --> 00:16:13,180
(I miss you so much)

489
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:14,270
Use an umbrella.

490
00:16:14,270 --> 00:16:16,060
(What do I do when it rains?
Just use an umbrella)

491
00:16:20,460 --> 00:16:21,380
Okay.

492
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:21,700
That works.

493
00:16:22,140 --> 00:16:24,180
(Passed)

494
00:16:24,510 --> 00:16:26,430
The second keyword is I.

495
00:16:26,430 --> 00:16:29,300
(Second keyword: I)

496
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:30,950
When I remove my mascara.

497
00:16:31,580 --> 00:16:33,060
(Searches his song library)

498
00:16:33,430 --> 00:16:34,510
(Search failed)
What song is that?

499
00:16:35,110 --> 00:16:36,140
(When I remove my mascara, Jolin Tsai)
It's a real song.

500
00:16:36,140 --> 00:16:37,910
(Xing gets one right)
It is.

501
00:16:37,910 --> 00:16:38,420
Three.

502
00:16:43,830 --> 00:16:44,870
What do I do when it rains?

503
00:16:44,870 --> 00:16:47,030
I miss you so much

504
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:52,580
(Bohan gets one right)

505
00:16:55,670 --> 00:16:57,230
Hey, I already used that one.

506
00:16:57,230 --> 00:16:58,060
(Strict)

507
00:16:58,230 --> 00:16:59,590
But you didn't sing the last line.

508
00:17:00,350 --> 00:17:00,910
Right?

509
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:02,940
Fine.

510
00:17:04,950 --> 00:17:06,190
Does that count as passing?

511
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:08,900
(Three correct answers,
fridge magnets unlocked)

512
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:09,560
(Xing and Bohan's
Eyes-Closed Guessing Game)

513
00:17:09,560 --> 00:17:10,660
(One closes their eyes while the other
brushes an object against their hand)

514
00:17:10,660 --> 00:17:11,080
(They get three guesses)

515
00:17:11,080 --> 00:17:11,980
(Guess correctly to unlock
three pairs of mini plates)

516
00:17:11,980 --> 00:17:13,420
(Guesser, Clue giver)

517
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:17,460
(Chooses a blueberry)

518
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:23,380
(Feeling it)

519
00:17:23,740 --> 00:17:24,180
A brush?

520
00:17:24,180 --> 00:17:24,980
No.

521
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:26,820
(Finds it funny)

522
00:17:26,860 --> 00:17:28,300
(Feels it again)

523
00:17:28,510 --> 00:17:29,430
It's wet.

524
00:17:30,030 --> 00:17:31,660
It doesn't have to be.

525
00:17:32,980 --> 00:17:34,260
What?

526
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:35,630
Let me feel

527
00:17:35,630 --> 00:17:37,190
the whole thing properly.

528
00:17:38,310 --> 00:17:39,110
That's all there is.

529
00:17:39,110 --> 00:17:39,900
Yeah.

530
00:17:40,150 --> 00:17:41,900
Is it the tip of a paintbrush?

531
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:42,700
No.

532
00:17:45,150 --> 00:17:45,820
I didn't look.

533
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:46,430
I really didn't.

534
00:17:46,430 --> 00:17:47,380
(Laughs so hard she bends over)

535
00:17:51,350 --> 00:17:52,430
This shape...

536
00:17:53,830 --> 00:17:55,110
What is it?

537
00:17:55,260 --> 00:17:56,350
I'm laughing so hard I'm crying.

538
00:17:59,350 --> 00:17:59,980
Something you can eat.

539
00:17:59,980 --> 00:18:00,540
A blueberry.

540
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:01,340
(Correct)
Yes.

541
00:18:01,710 --> 00:18:03,390
Wait, where did you get a blueberry?

542
00:18:03,980 --> 00:18:04,780
Here.

543
00:18:09,950 --> 00:18:10,830
Now you guess one.

544
00:18:10,830 --> 00:18:11,630
Okay.

545
00:18:11,630 --> 00:18:12,900
(Looking around)

546
00:18:15,780 --> 00:18:17,580
(Snickers)

547
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:19,940
(Chooses a blueberry too)

548
00:18:22,340 --> 00:18:23,380
(Touches)

549
00:18:23,380 --> 00:18:24,510
Can you guess it?

550
00:18:25,390 --> 00:18:27,150
Are you using this to get back at me?

551
00:18:30,190 --> 00:18:31,390
Can you guess?

552
00:18:31,390 --> 00:18:32,110
Try again.

553
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:39,900
(Pokes)

554
00:18:47,230 --> 00:18:48,590
(Taps repeatedly)
You keep tapping me with it.

555
00:18:53,990 --> 00:18:55,140
Is it a pen?

556
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:55,830
No.

557
00:18:55,830 --> 00:18:56,420
(First guess is wrong)

558
00:18:56,670 --> 00:18:58,580
It feels like

559
00:18:58,580 --> 00:19:00,310
your hand is pretty close to mine.

560
00:19:00,590 --> 00:19:02,390
So it can't be very long, right?

561
00:19:02,420 --> 00:19:03,220
(Good reasoning)
Right.

562
00:19:03,550 --> 00:19:05,020
It's something on the table, right?

563
00:19:05,020 --> 00:19:05,620
Yes.

564
00:19:05,620 --> 00:19:06,470
A paintbrush?

565
00:19:06,470 --> 00:19:07,260
No.

566
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:08,540
