701
00:23:38,190 --> 00:23:38,430
Yeah.

702
00:23:38,430 --> 00:23:39,390
It'll look even better.

703
00:23:40,790 --> 00:23:42,830
Your blue will look great
after it's fired too.

704
00:23:42,830 --> 00:23:43,820
A soft blue.

705
00:23:43,820 --> 00:23:45,660
Like denim blue.

706
00:23:45,990 --> 00:23:47,390
That color looks really good on you.

707
00:23:47,390 --> 00:23:47,820
Really?

708
00:23:47,820 --> 00:23:49,020
Light denim blue.

709
00:23:49,020 --> 00:23:51,180
Yeah. Your lucky blue outfit, right?

710
00:23:51,180 --> 00:23:53,020
You were wearing blue
the first time I saw you too.

711
00:23:53,020 --> 00:23:54,550
Blue is my

712
00:23:54,550 --> 00:23:55,630
lucky color.

713
00:23:55,700 --> 00:23:56,900
(Blue is my lucky color)

714
00:23:57,110 --> 00:23:59,180
At first, I thought green
was my lucky color.

715
00:23:59,180 --> 00:24:00,500
Green is your favorite color.

716
00:24:00,500 --> 00:24:02,110
Yeah. Green is my favorite color.

717
00:24:02,110 --> 00:24:03,300
Blue is my lucky color.

718
00:24:03,870 --> 00:24:06,550
I hope I can use my lucky color

719
00:24:06,550 --> 00:24:07,550
and...

720
00:24:07,550 --> 00:24:08,550
Pass some luck on to everyone.

721
00:24:08,550 --> 00:24:09,100
Right.

722
00:24:20,350 --> 00:24:22,350
Yours still looks better.

723
00:24:22,420 --> 00:24:23,620
(Glances)

724
00:24:23,620 --> 00:24:25,190
Yours is simple and classy.

725
00:24:26,270 --> 00:24:27,790
We've got one last one.

726
00:24:27,820 --> 00:24:29,620
Let's keep this one simple.

727
00:24:29,620 --> 00:24:30,020
Okay.

728
00:24:32,620 --> 00:24:34,020
(Focused and serious)

729
00:24:37,550 --> 00:24:38,350
Okay.

730
00:24:39,590 --> 00:24:40,590
We're done.

731
00:24:40,590 --> 00:24:42,630
All six plates are finished.

732
00:24:42,630 --> 00:24:43,430
Yeah.

733
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:46,670
The magnets are baked.

734
00:24:46,670 --> 00:24:47,550
Let's start coloring them.

735
00:24:52,950 --> 00:24:54,870
Once you fill it all in and bake it,
it'll be colorful.

736
00:24:54,870 --> 00:24:56,550
You're highlighting the star first.

737
00:24:56,550 --> 00:24:58,470
Yeah. I'm highlighting the star first.

738
00:25:01,460 --> 00:25:02,580
(Glances)

739
00:25:05,030 --> 00:25:06,310
The colors look really good.

740
00:25:07,310 --> 00:25:08,990
Yours too. You painted it so carefully.

741
00:25:08,990 --> 00:25:10,870
With you being this detail-oriented,

742
00:25:10,870 --> 00:25:12,940
I can't fall behind, right?

743
00:25:14,750 --> 00:25:15,870
Yours is so detailed.

744
00:25:17,140 --> 00:25:17,940
Okay.

745
00:25:22,020 --> 00:25:22,860
(Smiles)

746
00:25:24,030 --> 00:25:25,070
Looks good.

747
00:25:29,710 --> 00:25:30,710
Okay, that's it.

748
00:25:30,710 --> 00:25:31,190
Okay.

749
00:25:31,190 --> 00:25:33,510
Let's take a few photos
for everyone too.

750
00:25:33,510 --> 00:25:33,780
Okay.

751
00:25:33,990 --> 00:25:35,350
I'll take a photo of you first.

752
00:25:36,470 --> 00:25:37,070
I'll do this.

753
00:25:37,070 --> 00:25:38,070
Then you do this.

754
00:25:38,860 --> 00:25:39,660
(Agrees right away)
Sure.

755
00:25:39,860 --> 00:25:40,820
One.

756
00:25:40,820 --> 00:25:41,740
Two.

757
00:25:41,740 --> 00:25:42,300
Three.

758
00:25:44,820 --> 00:25:45,780
Three.

759
00:25:45,780 --> 00:25:46,460
Two.

760
00:25:46,460 --> 00:25:46,860
One.

761
00:25:51,270 --> 00:25:52,230
(Moves closer)
So good.

762
00:25:52,830 --> 00:25:54,340
Let's take some together too.

763
00:25:54,340 --> 00:25:54,660
Sure.

764
00:25:56,460 --> 00:25:56,900
Let's do it.

765
00:25:57,900 --> 00:25:58,540
Let's do it.

766
00:26:05,100 --> 00:26:06,220
Three.

767
00:26:06,220 --> 00:26:06,900
Two.

768
00:26:06,900 --> 00:26:07,460
One.

769
00:26:11,630 --> 00:26:13,350
There's a rose over there.

770
00:26:14,190 --> 00:26:15,910
It matches your outfit perfectly.

771
00:26:18,300 --> 00:26:21,140
Three, two, one.

772
00:26:24,100 --> 00:26:25,900
(Surprise polaroid drop)

773
00:26:30,820 --> 00:26:31,500
Nice.

774
00:26:35,260 --> 00:26:36,940
(Focused)

775
00:26:43,380 --> 00:26:44,340
(Sneaks a peek)

776
00:26:46,220 --> 00:26:47,460
(Smiles)

777
00:26:47,460 --> 00:26:49,030
(Wu Xingying's note)
Stars come out at night.

778
00:26:51,380 --> 00:26:52,660
(Shy)

779
00:26:52,660 --> 00:26:54,390
Eat on time and stay happy.

780
00:26:54,750 --> 00:26:55,870
(Eat on time and stay happy)
That's done.

781
00:26:55,870 --> 00:26:57,070
(Be confident, brave, and sincere)
Let's start packing now.

782
00:26:57,070 --> 00:26:57,750
Okay.

783
00:27:05,150 --> 00:27:06,430
Looks good.

784
00:27:08,230 --> 00:27:09,500
Is there enough around the edges?

785
00:27:09,500 --> 00:27:10,230
Yeah.

786
00:27:10,230 --> 00:27:11,070
There's a pillow too.

787
00:27:17,790 --> 00:27:19,070
Then...

788
00:27:19,830 --> 00:27:20,900
Lift it a little higher.

789
00:27:20,900 --> 00:27:21,540
A little higher?

790
00:27:21,540 --> 00:27:21,910
Yeah.

791
00:27:29,270 --> 00:27:30,990
Okay, put it down.

792
00:27:30,990 --> 00:27:32,270
I'll hold this side for you.

793
00:27:35,460 --> 00:27:37,030
You've clearly done this before.

794
00:27:37,910 --> 00:27:39,310
You can do everything.

795
00:27:40,620 --> 00:27:41,420
Okay.

796
00:27:41,990 --> 00:27:44,300
To everyone who gets these gifts,

797
00:27:44,300 --> 00:27:45,070
hope you're happy every day.

798
00:27:45,270 --> 00:27:46,900
And stay healthy and safe.

799
00:27:46,900 --> 00:27:49,020
Hope you like them. Bye.

800
00:27:49,020 --> 00:27:49,740
Bye.

801
00:27:49,780 --> 00:27:54,740
(Behind-the-Scenes 3)

802
00:27:54,780 --> 00:27:57,700
(Behind-the-Scenes, humming)

803
00:27:58,750 --> 00:28:00,070
When you were little,

804
00:28:00,260 --> 00:28:01,740
did you grow up with your parents?

805
00:28:01,740 --> 00:28:02,190
(Curious)
Yeah.

806
00:28:03,580 --> 00:28:05,590
Do you see your grandpa often?

807
00:28:06,270 --> 00:28:07,260
Whenever I go back there,

808
00:28:07,260 --> 00:28:08,630
I go see my grandpa.

809
00:28:10,340 --> 00:28:13,060
I grew up with my grandma.

810
00:28:13,700 --> 00:28:14,900
Until I was six.

811
00:28:16,830 --> 00:28:19,270
Then I came back

812
00:28:19,510 --> 00:28:20,910
and started dancing.

813
00:28:21,270 --> 00:28:22,950
So you started really young.

814
00:28:23,910 --> 00:28:26,230
You've basically trained
since childhood.

815
00:28:26,830 --> 00:28:28,390
I think things you learn that young

816
00:28:28,390 --> 00:28:30,110
just become part of you.

817
00:28:30,580 --> 00:28:31,180
Yeah.

818
00:28:32,030 --> 00:28:33,790
I still want my grandma

819
00:28:34,230 --> 00:28:35,710
to live with us.

820
00:28:35,710 --> 00:28:38,190
But she still prefers living on her own.

821
00:28:38,740 --> 00:28:41,900
I feel like older people
need someone around.

822
00:28:41,990 --> 00:28:42,590
Yeah.

823
00:28:42,590 --> 00:28:45,340
Maybe someday she'll change her mind

824
00:28:45,340 --> 00:28:46,140
and agree.

825
00:28:46,470 --> 00:28:48,750
I think

826
00:28:48,750 --> 00:28:53,310
that generation really gave so much.

827
00:28:53,310 --> 00:28:55,790
When it comes to love, I feel like...

828
00:28:56,030 --> 00:28:56,990
They sacrificed so much.

829
00:28:56,990 --> 00:28:58,310
Yeah, so much.

830
00:28:58,670 --> 00:29:00,750
And they never expect anything back.

831
00:29:00,860 --> 00:29:01,740
(Selfless love)
They just give.

832
00:29:01,860 --> 00:29:02,300
Yeah.

833
00:29:02,430 --> 00:29:03,030
Exactly.

834
00:29:03,860 --> 00:29:08,820
(Behind-the-Scenes 4)

835
00:29:08,860 --> 00:29:11,900
(Behind-the-Scenes)

836
00:29:11,900 --> 00:29:12,820
Hi.

837
00:29:14,700 --> 00:29:15,340
(Smiles)

838
00:29:15,550 --> 00:29:16,430
You've already started?

839
00:29:17,460 --> 00:29:18,300
Yeah, already started.

840
00:29:19,790 --> 00:29:20,470
You eat first.

841
00:29:20,470 --> 00:29:21,270
I'm waiting for the toast.

842
00:29:21,270 --> 00:29:22,310
No, let's eat together.

843
00:29:22,550 --> 00:29:23,340
Okay.

844
00:29:25,700 --> 00:29:27,060
(Glances)

845
00:29:28,590 --> 00:29:30,470
Did you flip the egg or anything?

846
00:29:30,910 --> 00:29:32,150
It just cooked like this?

847
00:29:33,510 --> 00:29:33,870
What?

848
00:29:34,430 --> 00:29:35,750
It cooked all the way like this?

849
00:29:36,310 --> 00:29:37,430
That's pretty impressive.

850
00:29:37,430 --> 00:29:38,710
(Impressed)
How would you even flip it?

851
00:29:38,710 --> 00:29:40,150
Before, the top looked cooked,

852
00:29:40,150 --> 00:29:41,230
but it was raw inside.

853
00:29:41,870 --> 00:29:43,910
So maybe it needed
another round in the oven.

854
00:29:44,350 --> 00:29:45,350
I just tried some.

855
00:29:45,350 --> 00:29:46,190
It's all cooked.

856
00:29:46,310 --> 00:29:47,110
Is it done?

857
00:29:47,670 --> 00:29:48,110
It's done?

858
00:29:49,590 --> 00:29:51,030
Then the timing must've been just right.

859
00:29:52,140 --> 00:29:53,620
(Smiles)

860
00:29:54,260 --> 00:29:54,660
Let's go.

861
00:30:00,940 --> 00:30:01,620
Let's eat first.

862
00:30:01,940 --> 00:30:03,180
(Looks closely)

863
00:30:03,180 --> 00:30:05,630
You got it kinda like an onsen egg.

864
00:30:06,190 --> 00:30:06,950
Soft in the middle.

865
00:30:06,950 --> 00:30:07,750
Try it.

866
00:30:11,030 --> 00:30:11,550
It's good.

867
00:30:12,940 --> 00:30:14,430
Can you taste a little sweetness inside?

868
00:30:14,430 --> 00:30:15,350
(Pays attention)

869
00:30:15,350 --> 00:30:16,070
Is there sugar inside?

870
00:30:16,630 --> 00:30:17,180
I added

871
00:30:17,180 --> 00:30:17,940
some honey.

872
00:30:22,070 --> 00:30:23,230
I didn't know if you'd used it before.

873
00:30:24,350 --> 00:30:24,870
I hadn't.

874
00:30:24,870 --> 00:30:26,110
But honey actually tastes really good.

875
00:30:26,110 --> 00:30:27,350
I'll make it for you again next time.

876
00:30:27,350 --> 00:30:27,860
Okay.

877
00:30:28,460 --> 00:30:33,420
(Behind-the-Scenes 5)

878
00:30:33,860 --> 00:30:34,780
(Behind-the-Scenes)
I'm really sleepy.

879
00:30:34,990 --> 00:30:36,150
Is there a coffee machine?

880
00:30:36,550 --> 00:30:37,910
Yeah, definitely.

881
00:30:38,550 --> 00:30:39,790
How do you use it?

882
00:30:40,670 --> 00:30:42,190
I think we need to plug it in.

883
00:31:00,150 --> 00:31:01,230
What's going on?

884
00:31:02,950 --> 00:31:03,990
Can it actually make coffee?

885
00:31:03,990 --> 00:31:05,510
(Joking)
It's not gonna explode, is it?

886
00:31:05,870 --> 00:31:07,740
If it explodes, let's back up.

887
00:31:07,740 --> 00:31:08,460
I'm not scared.

888
00:31:08,460 --> 00:31:09,190
You're not?

889
00:31:09,190 --> 00:31:10,350
I'm scared you'll get hurt.

890
00:31:10,820 --> 00:31:11,740
(Smiles)

891
00:31:13,140 --> 00:31:14,500
(Leaking)

892
00:31:15,110 --> 00:31:15,740
I think it's broken.

893
00:31:15,740 --> 00:31:16,420
Okay, stop.

894
00:31:16,630 --> 00:31:18,030
(Wrecking the place)
You look like you're wrecking the place.

895
00:31:18,030 --> 00:31:18,940
Stop.

896
00:31:18,940 --> 00:31:20,260
(Damage control)

897
00:31:23,790 --> 00:31:24,980
Is there more?

898
00:31:24,980 --> 00:31:25,950
Yeah.

899
00:31:25,950 --> 00:31:27,110
But I'm not sure.

900
00:31:27,750 --> 00:31:29,310
Maybe it's because it's
my first time using it.

901
00:31:29,310 --> 00:31:30,700
I might be doing it wrong.

902
00:31:30,700 --> 00:31:32,390
So far, it looks right.

903
00:31:32,390 --> 00:31:33,870
It's even giving us plain hot water.

904
00:31:33,870 --> 00:31:34,620
(Plain water)

905
00:31:35,910 --> 00:31:37,550
Might as well have some warm water.

906
00:31:38,260 --> 00:31:38,940
Fail.

907
00:31:39,620 --> 00:31:40,860
(Cracks up)

908
00:31:40,860 --> 00:31:41,590
At least it's...

909
00:31:41,590 --> 00:31:42,990
This looks really bitter.

910
00:31:42,990 --> 00:31:43,780
At least it's black.

911
00:31:43,780 --> 00:31:45,150
So we can't be totally wrong.

912
00:31:46,670 --> 00:31:48,390
Still don't know
if we did it right, though.

913
00:31:50,260 --> 00:31:55,220
(Behind-the-Scenes 6)

914
00:31:55,260 --> 00:31:57,860
(Behind-the-Scenes)

915
00:31:57,860 --> 00:31:59,950
The amusement park must've been fun.

916
00:32:00,430 --> 00:32:02,110
It had a lot of thrill rides.

917
00:32:02,110 --> 00:32:02,990
Yeah.

918
00:32:02,990 --> 00:32:03,900
For thrill rides,

919
00:32:03,900 --> 00:32:05,950
there were like three
or four roller coasters.

920
00:32:05,950 --> 00:32:07,910
And they were all pretty intense.

921
00:32:08,430 --> 00:32:09,870
So none of you get scared?

922
00:32:10,380 --> 00:32:11,220
Are you scared?

923
00:32:11,220 --> 00:32:11,940
No.

924
00:32:12,860 --> 00:32:15,420
We should all go
to Happy Valley sometime.

925
00:32:15,420 --> 00:32:16,470
That'd be awesome.

926
00:32:17,580 --> 00:32:19,070
Did you eat anything good?

927
00:32:19,670 --> 00:32:21,140
The place we went
for dinner was pretty good.

928
00:32:21,140 --> 00:32:22,300
There was this...

929
00:32:22,740 --> 00:32:23,540
(Swallows)

930
00:32:23,540 --> 00:32:24,790
Let me swallow first.

931
00:32:25,430 --> 00:32:26,310
It

932
00:32:26,310 --> 00:32:28,790
was some kind of hot-and-sour chicken.

933
00:32:29,470 --> 00:32:32,070
And there was sticky rice.
It smelled amazing.

934
00:32:32,270 --> 00:32:33,950
It already sounds delicious.

935
00:32:33,950 --> 00:32:34,590
Yeah.

936
00:32:34,590 --> 00:32:36,220
Then there was beef risotto,

937
00:32:36,220 --> 00:32:37,790
and bone marrow rice.

938
00:32:39,310 --> 00:32:40,110
Highly recommend it.

939
00:32:42,580 --> 00:32:43,380
So good.

940
00:32:43,630 --> 00:32:45,310
Okay, I'll try it next time.

941
00:32:45,740 --> 00:32:50,700
(Behind-the-Scenes 7)

942
00:32:51,060 --> 00:32:51,980
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Take a shot. Come on.

943
00:32:51,980 --> 00:32:53,830
Come on. Set one up for me.

944
00:32:54,230 --> 00:32:56,550
Let's see how "nice" you are.

945
00:32:56,870 --> 00:32:57,590
Hit this red ball.

946
00:32:57,590 --> 00:32:58,310
Thanks.

947
00:33:00,270 --> 00:33:00,750
(Sinks it)
Nice.

948
00:33:01,190 --> 00:33:02,270
(Compliments)
You set it up well.

949
00:33:02,430 --> 00:33:03,430
Okay, your turn.

950
00:33:07,980 --> 00:33:08,700
(Banks it in)

951
00:33:09,830 --> 00:33:10,740
Yes.

952
00:33:10,740 --> 00:33:12,420
You can go straight for the blue ball.

953
00:33:15,780 --> 00:33:17,180
(Thinking)

954
00:33:18,390 --> 00:33:19,230
Time to calculate.

955
00:33:38,740 --> 00:33:39,540
I'll do it.

956
00:33:41,900 --> 00:33:42,860
That's kinda scary.

957
00:33:44,030 --> 00:33:45,430
Seriously, your shots are kinda scary.

958
00:33:46,390 --> 00:33:47,470
This is the only one I can hit.

959
00:33:49,390 --> 00:33:49,900
Okay, like that.

960
00:33:49,900 --> 00:33:51,660
I feel like you're about to win, right?

961
00:33:51,660 --> 00:33:52,670
Quick, take the shot.

962
00:33:52,670 --> 00:33:54,830
Thanks. Did you let me win just now?

963
00:33:54,830 --> 00:33:55,350
No.

964
00:33:55,350 --> 00:33:56,420
I gave it my all.

965
00:33:59,670 --> 00:34:00,700
If you're gonna let me win like this,

966
00:34:00,700 --> 00:34:02,230
there's nothing I can do.

967
00:34:02,230 --> 00:34:03,990
The suspense continues.

968
00:34:14,580 --> 00:34:15,219
Here.

969
00:34:15,260 --> 00:34:16,060
Okay.

970
00:34:19,860 --> 00:34:20,260
Yes.

971
00:34:20,260 --> 00:34:21,020
Thanks.

972
00:34:21,020 --> 00:34:21,820
You won.

973
00:34:23,380 --> 00:34:28,340
(Behind-the-Scenes 8)

974
00:34:28,630 --> 00:34:30,030
(Behind-the-Scenes)
I'll get you some water.

975
00:34:30,030 --> 00:34:30,820
Okay.

976
00:34:32,420 --> 00:34:33,070
Is it hot?

977
00:34:35,230 --> 00:34:35,860
No.

978
00:34:35,860 --> 00:34:36,620
I mixed in some

979
00:34:36,620 --> 00:34:39,500
(Moves closer)
water at 25, 45, 85, and 99 degrees.

980
00:34:40,230 --> 00:34:40,989
(Smiles)
That many?

981
00:34:42,469 --> 00:34:43,590
You're really not cold?

982
00:34:43,750 --> 00:34:45,469
No. This is a sweater.

983
00:34:45,670 --> 00:34:47,630
Did you take
your cold medicine yesterday?

984
00:34:47,870 --> 00:34:48,550
(Concerned)
No.

985
00:34:48,900 --> 00:34:49,179
I forgot.

986
00:34:49,179 --> 00:34:49,989
Then why didn't you take it?

987
00:34:49,989 --> 00:34:51,230
Because you didn't remind me.

988
00:34:51,710 --> 00:34:52,989
I did remind you.

989
00:34:56,380 --> 00:34:57,580
I'll go in a bit.

990
00:34:58,670 --> 00:34:59,990
I'll definitely take it today.

991
00:35:00,470 --> 00:35:01,860
(Promises)
I'll put it in my cup.

992
00:35:01,860 --> 00:35:02,950
I'll finish this first.

993
00:35:02,950 --> 00:35:03,950
Then get me a cup of hot water.

994
00:35:03,950 --> 00:35:04,750
I'll mix it right away.

995
00:35:06,710 --> 00:35:07,460
Okay?

996
00:35:07,460 --> 00:35:08,260
Okay.

997
00:35:08,260 --> 00:35:09,750
But today I really don't...

998
00:35:10,390 --> 00:35:11,150
I just feel better.

999
00:35:13,790 --> 00:35:15,230
You should still be careful.

1000
00:35:16,260 --> 00:35:21,220
(Behind-the-Scenes 9)

1001
00:35:21,260 --> 00:35:27,420
(Behind-the-Scenes)

1002
00:35:27,420 --> 00:35:28,910
(Concerned)
How are you? Feeling better?

1003
00:35:29,220 --> 00:35:29,900
A little better.

1004
00:35:30,420 --> 00:35:31,740
That's good.

1005
00:35:31,830 --> 00:35:33,590
She probably just needs

1006
00:35:34,350 --> 00:35:35,310
to rest and recover.

1007
00:35:35,310 --> 00:35:35,750
Yeah.

1008
00:35:36,580 --> 00:35:37,180
I feel like

1009
00:35:37,630 --> 00:35:38,870
I haven't gotten

1010
00:35:38,870 --> 00:35:40,790
enough time with her in the house.

1011
00:35:40,790 --> 00:35:41,510
No rush.

1012
00:35:41,510 --> 00:35:42,710
It doesn't have

1013
00:35:42,710 --> 00:35:44,180
to end just because our time

1014
00:35:44,180 --> 00:35:45,140
in the house

1015
00:35:45,140 --> 00:35:45,700
ends,

1016
00:35:45,700 --> 00:35:46,300
right?

1017
00:35:47,150 --> 00:35:48,350
Look at it another way.

1018
00:35:48,540 --> 00:35:49,820
Getting to meet her here

1019
00:35:49,820 --> 00:35:51,300
(Meeting itself is a kind of luck)
was already lucky in itself.

1020
00:35:52,790 --> 00:35:53,470
I get it.

1021
00:35:53,470 --> 00:35:54,550
I just feel bad for her...

1022
00:35:55,390 --> 00:35:56,710
because it's a little unfortunate

1023
00:35:56,710 --> 00:35:57,380
that she

1024
00:35:57,380 --> 00:35:58,060
got sick.

1025
00:35:59,270 --> 00:36:01,390
Her missing out hurts me more
than my own regret.

1026
00:36:01,790 --> 00:36:02,830
Don't overthink it.

1027
00:36:03,030 --> 00:36:04,630
Take her rowing more when she gets back.

1028
00:36:05,910 --> 00:36:06,710
Right?

1029
00:36:07,550 --> 00:36:08,700
Just have fun

1030
00:36:08,700 --> 00:36:09,670
and spend

1031
00:36:09,670 --> 00:36:10,750
more time with her.

1032
00:36:10,750 --> 00:36:12,590
Then we'll wait for her to come back.

1033
00:36:14,190 --> 00:36:15,590
She'll be back soon, right?

1034
00:36:15,910 --> 00:36:17,350
She can feel how much you care.

1035
00:36:17,470 --> 00:36:18,550
Don't overthink it.

1036
00:36:19,230 --> 00:36:20,790
It's okay. I'm much better now.

1037
00:36:21,980 --> 00:36:26,940
(Behind-the-Scenes 10)

1038
00:36:26,980 --> 00:36:28,220
(Behind-the-Scenes)

1039
00:36:28,220 --> 00:36:29,430
The bottom's already burnt.

1040
00:36:30,140 --> 00:36:31,780
(Making celery beef)

1041
00:36:33,140 --> 00:36:34,300
(Choked by the fumes +1)

1042
00:36:35,340 --> 00:36:36,740
(Choked by the fumes +2)

1043
00:36:37,820 --> 00:36:39,100
(Source of the fumes)

1044
00:36:39,460 --> 00:36:40,660
(Gets choked too)

1045
00:36:40,750 --> 00:36:41,740
Is the range hood off?

1046
00:36:41,740 --> 00:36:42,980
It's on.

1047
00:36:42,980 --> 00:36:44,020
Yeah, it's on.

1048
00:36:44,700 --> 00:36:45,750
Sorry.

1049
00:36:46,870 --> 00:36:48,110
Hold on. I'm gonna step away.

1050
00:36:49,310 --> 00:36:50,060
I'm almost done.

1051
00:36:50,060 --> 00:36:50,860
Almost done.

1052
00:36:51,260 --> 00:36:51,860
Almost.

1053
00:36:51,860 --> 00:36:52,740
Okay.

1054
00:36:53,620 --> 00:36:54,380
(Covers mouth)

1055
00:36:55,060 --> 00:36:55,860
(Glances)

1056
00:36:56,100 --> 00:36:57,220
(Fans the air)

1057
00:37:00,830 --> 00:37:02,030
It's okay.

1058
00:37:02,030 --> 00:37:03,350
(Compliments)
It already looks delicious.

1059
00:37:07,270 --> 00:37:09,270
It smells amazing.

1060
00:37:09,270 --> 00:37:10,750
It's gotta be good.

1061
00:37:11,870 --> 00:37:13,030
Almost. Just a sec.

1062
00:37:16,750 --> 00:37:17,830
It's done.

1063
00:37:17,860 --> 00:37:19,340
(Ready to serve)

1064
00:37:19,340 --> 00:37:21,270
Cui Yihang worked really hard today,

1065
00:37:21,270 --> 00:37:22,990
making such a big spread.

1066
00:37:23,540 --> 00:37:24,270
Here are your noodles.

1067
00:37:24,270 --> 00:37:25,030
Thanks.

1068
00:37:30,950 --> 00:37:32,460
So good. You guys made this really well.

1069
00:37:33,950 --> 00:37:35,110
I wanna steal a bite of this.

1070
00:37:35,910 --> 00:37:36,740
Let me steal a bite.

1071
00:37:36,740 --> 00:37:37,470
Go ahead.

1072
00:37:37,470 --> 00:37:38,660
Why don't you take some?

1073
00:37:38,660 --> 00:37:39,180
Take some.

1074
00:37:39,180 --> 00:37:40,190
Scoop some out.

1075
00:37:40,190 --> 00:37:41,510
Let me taste how spicy it is first.

1076
00:37:46,260 --> 00:37:46,980
How is it?

1077
00:37:47,650 --> 00:37:48,230
Nice.

1078
00:37:51,460 --> 00:37:56,420
(Behind-the-Scenes 11)

1079
00:37:56,460 --> 00:37:59,060
(Behind-the-Scenes)

1080
00:37:59,060 --> 00:37:59,940
(Checks the wound)

1081
00:37:59,940 --> 00:38:01,020
It's bleeding.

1082
00:38:03,190 --> 00:38:04,470
Let's go upstairs and get some medicine.

1083
00:38:04,470 --> 00:38:05,430
Let's treat it now.

1084
00:38:05,430 --> 00:38:06,030
Let's go.

1085
00:38:06,030 --> 00:38:07,220
(Laughs)

1086
00:38:07,750 --> 00:38:08,390
Okay.

1087
00:38:10,670 --> 00:38:11,340
Where should we do it?

1088
00:38:11,340 --> 00:38:11,580
Right here.

1089
00:38:11,580 --> 00:38:12,420
I'll take it out.

1090
00:38:12,420 --> 00:38:12,990
Go ahead.

1091
00:38:13,460 --> 00:38:16,100
(Waits for Fang to get the medicine)

1092
00:38:19,630 --> 00:38:20,300
Sit here.

1093
00:38:20,710 --> 00:38:23,590
Let's treat it.

1094
00:38:23,980 --> 00:38:24,700
(Careful)

1095
00:38:24,740 --> 00:38:26,020
(Helps treat the wound)

1096
00:38:26,020 --> 00:38:27,630
If we're disinfecting it,

1097
00:38:27,630 --> 00:38:29,190
we can clean around the edges too.

1098
00:38:31,350 --> 00:38:32,470
I'll get some tissues.

1099
00:38:36,660 --> 00:38:38,620
(Kneels on one knee)

1100
00:38:40,190 --> 00:38:41,910
(Smiles)
Let me switch positions.

1101
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:44,730
Oh my God.

1102
00:38:45,710 --> 00:38:47,590
You're putting me
under so much pressure.

1103
00:38:47,670 --> 00:38:49,670
This position's just more comfortable.

1104
00:38:49,940 --> 00:38:51,020
(Laughs)

1105
00:38:51,420 --> 00:38:52,740
(Carefully treats the wound)

1106
00:38:53,630 --> 00:38:54,870
Let's get some gauze.

1107
00:38:56,630 --> 00:38:58,660
(Teases)
Let me think how Peking duck is wrapped.

1108
00:39:00,310 --> 00:39:01,670
How is that even the same thing?

1109
00:39:07,670 --> 00:39:09,270
Okay. Success.

1110
00:39:12,430 --> 00:39:13,580
Thanks,

1111
00:39:13,580 --> 00:39:15,060
Dr. Yu.

1112
00:39:16,940 --> 00:39:21,900
(Behind-the-Scenes 12)

1113
00:39:21,900 --> 00:39:23,100
(Behind-the-Scenes)

1114
00:39:23,100 --> 00:39:23,820
(Thinking)

1115
00:39:23,820 --> 00:39:25,430
I can instantly give myself
double eyelids.

1116
00:39:25,430 --> 00:39:26,230
Let me see. Go.

1117
00:39:26,230 --> 00:39:26,620
(Excited)

1118
00:39:32,140 --> 00:39:34,260
(Cracks up)

1119
00:39:35,750 --> 00:39:38,830
I make the crease
by folding it like this.

1120
00:39:38,830 --> 00:39:40,110
Just fold the skin over.

1121
00:39:44,340 --> 00:39:45,220
(Makes eye contact)

1122
00:39:46,940 --> 00:39:47,660
Impressive.

1123
00:39:48,230 --> 00:39:50,710
My friend says it looks really ugly.

1124
00:39:50,950 --> 00:39:52,220
I won't let him say that.

1125
00:39:52,580 --> 00:39:53,830
I won't let him say that.

1126
00:39:54,020 --> 00:39:54,860
(Smiles)

1127
00:39:54,860 --> 00:39:55,750
Say that.

1128
00:39:57,150 --> 00:39:58,230
He told me not to do it anymore.

1129
00:39:58,230 --> 00:39:59,350
No, it's not ugly.

1130
00:40:01,820 --> 00:40:02,580
Really.

1131
00:40:03,940 --> 00:40:06,740
Look, I got these red spots today.

1132
00:40:06,740 --> 00:40:07,550
What are they?

1133
00:40:08,150 --> 00:40:08,710
Why?

1134
00:40:08,710 --> 00:40:10,110
I had some on my neck last night too.

1135
00:40:12,100 --> 00:40:13,220
(Looks closely)

1136
00:40:13,220 --> 00:40:14,350
An allergic reaction?

1137
00:40:14,590 --> 00:40:15,980
I don't know. I don't feel anything.

1138
00:40:15,980 --> 00:40:16,790
It doesn't itch either.

1139
00:40:18,750 --> 00:40:19,740
Why is that?

1140
00:40:19,740 --> 00:40:20,590
Diagnose me.

1141
00:40:21,710 --> 00:40:24,030
Any other symptoms
to help with the diagnosis?

1142
00:40:24,030 --> 00:40:24,630
No symptoms at all.

1143
00:40:24,630 --> 00:40:25,830
There's one here too.

1144
00:40:26,150 --> 00:40:26,630
Here too?

1145
00:40:26,630 --> 00:40:28,390
Isn't this

1146
00:40:28,390 --> 00:40:28,910
a bug bite?

1147
00:40:30,150 --> 00:40:31,350
But I didn't feel anything.

1148
00:40:33,950 --> 00:40:35,510
I'll look it up for you tonight.

1149
00:40:38,940 --> 00:40:43,900
(Behind-the-Scenes 13)

1150
00:40:43,940 --> 00:40:45,340
(Behind-the-Scenes)

1151
00:40:45,340 --> 00:40:46,510
What do you want for breakfast tomorrow?

1152
00:40:49,310 --> 00:40:50,430
Anything's fine. Just tell me.

1153
00:40:50,430 --> 00:40:51,150
I can "make it appear" for you.

1154
00:40:51,700 --> 00:40:53,180
(Smiles)

1155
00:40:53,180 --> 00:40:53,910
You can "make it appear"?

1156
00:40:54,110 --> 00:40:54,790
Yeah.

1157
00:40:56,430 --> 00:40:57,830
Maybe a different kind of bread.

1158
00:40:59,030 --> 00:40:59,670
Sure.

1159
00:40:59,950 --> 00:41:00,670
Okay.

1160
00:41:01,310 --> 00:41:02,630
Just wait and eat.

1161
00:41:07,020 --> 00:41:07,420
Let's go.

1162
00:41:07,420 --> 00:41:08,270
Okay, let's go.

1163
00:41:09,990 --> 00:41:11,270
Those two must be kinda heavy.

1164
00:41:12,350 --> 00:41:13,340
- No, they're pretty light.
- It's fine. You go first.

1165
00:41:13,340 --> 00:41:13,750
Go.

1166
00:41:13,750 --> 00:41:14,670
You go first.

1167
00:41:14,990 --> 00:41:16,070
You're carrying more. You go first.

1168
00:41:16,070 --> 00:41:16,420
Go ahead.

1169
00:41:16,420 --> 00:41:17,230
You first.

1170
00:41:18,180 --> 00:41:18,630
This...

1171
00:41:18,630 --> 00:41:19,740
Let's go together.

1172
00:41:19,740 --> 00:41:20,540
Together.

1173
00:41:20,540 --> 00:41:22,340
(Walks together)

1174
00:41:22,340 --> 00:41:23,710
Why is there so much stuff?

1175
00:41:23,710 --> 00:41:26,270
Sun Bohan said he likes eating these.

1176
00:41:27,310 --> 00:41:27,910
Sun Bohan and Xing.

1177
00:41:27,910 --> 00:41:28,790
Xing got these for him?

1178
00:41:29,740 --> 00:41:31,100
(Food Xing brought for Sun Bohan)

1179
00:41:31,350 --> 00:41:32,710
Did they have anything to pass along

1180
00:41:32,710 --> 00:41:33,660
to each other today?

1181
00:41:33,660 --> 00:41:34,300
Xing.

1182
00:41:34,540 --> 00:41:34,900
She did.

1183
00:41:34,900 --> 00:41:35,540
She did, right?

1184
00:41:35,540 --> 00:41:36,700
I need to figure out how to say it.

1185
00:41:36,700 --> 00:41:37,660
Let me think.

1186
00:41:38,990 --> 00:41:39,390
Was it a lot?

1187
00:41:39,390 --> 00:41:40,790
She quizzed me a few times, like,

1188
00:41:41,190 --> 00:41:41,990
"Tell me again"

1189
00:41:41,990 --> 00:41:42,590
"what you're gonna tell him."

1190
00:41:42,590 --> 00:41:43,270
You had to recite it?

1191
00:41:43,420 --> 00:41:43,630
Yeah.

1192
00:41:43,630 --> 00:41:44,430
Then I forgot.

1193
00:41:44,430 --> 00:41:45,430
She said my head was empty

1194
00:41:45,430 --> 00:41:46,630
because I couldn't remember her message.

1195
00:41:46,630 --> 00:41:47,900
I probably shouldn't have talked
to you so much on the way back.

1196
00:41:47,900 --> 00:41:48,540
First, let me...

1197
00:41:49,150 --> 00:41:50,790
Practice it with me first.

1198
00:41:51,110 --> 00:41:52,220
You've got more stuff.

1199
00:41:52,220 --> 00:41:53,020
You go in first.

1200
00:41:53,020 --> 00:41:53,830
Okay.

1201
00:41:54,110 --> 00:41:54,910
Thanks.

1202
00:41:58,180 --> 00:42:03,140
(Behind-the-Scenes 14)

1203
00:42:03,590 --> 00:42:05,750
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Does everyone want some sticky notes?

1204
00:42:05,750 --> 00:42:06,980
(Getting ready to write wishes for Xing)
I think this one's prettier.

1205
00:42:07,500 --> 00:42:08,220
Sure.

1206
00:42:09,270 --> 00:42:10,180
Take two.

1207
00:42:10,180 --> 00:42:11,310
Thanks.

1208
00:42:11,910 --> 00:42:12,990
Take two more.

1209
00:42:13,340 --> 00:42:14,060
Okay.

1210
00:42:14,060 --> 00:42:14,950
Yu Yang,

1211
00:42:14,950 --> 00:42:16,910
these are for us to write to Xing.

1212
00:42:18,150 --> 00:42:19,310
Do you guys want some sticky notes?

1213
00:42:19,310 --> 00:42:20,110
We're writing wishes for Xing.

1214
00:42:20,830 --> 00:42:21,430
Sure.

1215
00:42:21,790 --> 00:42:23,910
Can we stick them on your door?

1216
00:42:23,910 --> 00:42:25,270
Yeah, sure.

1217
00:42:25,750 --> 00:42:27,950
Cui Yihang can collect the guys' notes.

1218
00:42:27,950 --> 00:42:29,550
You guys split them up.

1219
00:42:29,550 --> 00:42:30,550
Just split that stack.

1220
00:42:30,550 --> 00:42:31,340
Thanks.

1221
00:42:31,710 --> 00:42:32,790
Are they inside?

1222
00:42:32,790 --> 00:42:33,150
Yeah.

1223
00:42:33,150 --> 00:42:34,750
I'll take a few over to her.

1224
00:42:36,430 --> 00:42:37,230
Here I come.

1225
00:42:38,110 --> 00:42:39,950
Let's write Xing some notes.

1226
00:42:39,950 --> 00:42:40,750
No problem.

1227
00:42:40,750 --> 00:42:42,910
This stack should be enough.

1228
00:42:43,030 --> 00:42:43,340
Okay, sure.

1229
00:42:43,340 --> 00:42:43,620
Enough?

1230
00:42:43,620 --> 00:42:44,140
Yeah, that's fine.

1231
00:42:44,140 --> 00:42:44,740
Okay.

1232
00:42:44,860 --> 00:42:47,300
(Carefully writes their wishes)

1233
00:42:50,430 --> 00:42:52,030
Everyone's notes?

1234
00:42:52,030 --> 00:42:53,190
Okay, got it.

1235
00:42:53,190 --> 00:42:54,230
Just the guys'.

1236
00:42:54,230 --> 00:42:54,830
Yeah.

1237
00:42:54,830 --> 00:42:56,350
Okay, thanks.

1238
00:42:56,350 --> 00:42:57,220
Bye. Good night.

1239
00:42:57,220 --> 00:42:57,620
Good night.

1240
00:42:59,540 --> 00:43:04,500
(Behind-the-Scenes 15)

1241
00:43:04,540 --> 00:43:05,340
(Behind-the-Scenes)

1242
00:43:05,340 --> 00:43:07,270
Sit wherever. You can sit on the bed.

1243
00:43:07,270 --> 00:43:08,900
Did you go on a date today?

1244
00:43:08,900 --> 00:43:09,470
No.

1245
00:43:09,870 --> 00:43:10,550
You went by yourself?

1246
00:43:10,550 --> 00:43:11,380
Yeah.

1247
00:43:12,900 --> 00:43:14,500
(Chen Hewen's journal)

1248
00:43:15,670 --> 00:43:17,590
Can I see what you wrote about...

1249
00:43:17,910 --> 00:43:18,470
About who?

1250
00:43:19,430 --> 00:43:20,470
The info you wrote about Xing?

1251
00:43:20,470 --> 00:43:20,780
Yeah.

1252
00:43:20,780 --> 00:43:21,820
He might not have written any.

1253
00:43:22,230 --> 00:43:23,590
Xing came pretty late.

1254
00:43:23,750 --> 00:43:25,120
Isn't she Si's twin?

1255
00:43:25,120 --> 00:43:25,720
(They have things in common)

1256
00:43:26,660 --> 00:43:27,380
No.

1257
00:43:27,380 --> 00:43:28,550
So I wanna see her info.

1258
00:43:28,550 --> 00:43:29,550
You have Xing, right?

1259
00:43:30,350 --> 00:43:30,980
Mr. Cui.

1260
00:43:31,310 --> 00:43:32,190
Stop messing around.

1261
00:43:32,910 --> 00:43:34,590
Yiheng, Meng,

1262
00:43:34,590 --> 00:43:35,780
Yu Yang, Xing.

1263
00:43:35,780 --> 00:43:36,990
You wrote this much about Xing?

1264
00:43:38,630 --> 00:43:39,910
It's all exactly what she told me.

1265
00:43:39,940 --> 00:43:40,600
(Xing, Libra, INFJ)

1266
00:43:40,600 --> 00:43:41,820
(Badminton, runs an online clothing
business, Beijing, Northeast China)

1267
00:43:41,820 --> 00:43:43,060
(Focused)

1268
00:43:43,060 --> 00:43:44,430
They're both INFPs.

1269
00:43:46,830 --> 00:43:48,540
That's INFJ.

1270
00:43:48,820 --> 00:43:49,420
FJ.

1271
00:43:50,380 --> 00:43:51,590
I'm INFJ too.

1272
00:43:52,190 --> 00:43:53,070
We're only different by an I

1273
00:43:53,070 --> 00:43:53,870
and an E.

1274
00:43:54,350 --> 00:43:55,900
You're ENFP?

1275
00:43:55,900 --> 00:43:56,780
(Glances)
Yeah, ENFP.

1276
00:43:56,780 --> 00:43:57,540
(Glances again)

1277
00:43:57,540 --> 00:43:58,150
Are you outgoing?

1278
00:44:00,070 --> 00:44:01,100
Are you outgoing, Cui Yihang?

1279
00:44:01,100 --> 00:44:01,820
Are you?

1280
00:44:01,820 --> 00:44:02,460
Am I outgoing?

1281
00:44:02,460 --> 00:44:03,540
You'd know best.

1282
00:44:03,540 --> 00:44:04,910
You're pretty outgoing.

1283
00:44:05,940 --> 00:44:06,420
Okay.

1284
00:44:06,420 --> 00:44:07,550
I only wanna see her page.

1285
00:44:07,550 --> 00:44:08,150
Just one look.

1286
00:44:08,150 --> 00:44:09,110
Who do you wanna check out?

1287
00:44:09,310 --> 00:44:11,030
Just Si.

1288
00:44:13,790 --> 00:44:15,140
This is already super thoughtful.

1289
00:44:15,510 --> 00:44:16,350
I like observing people.

1290
00:44:16,740 --> 00:44:17,620
(Smiles)

1291
00:44:18,790 --> 00:44:19,830
Always volunteers to wash dishes.

1292
00:44:20,990 --> 00:44:21,590
Yeah.

1293
00:44:22,190 --> 00:44:24,110
I've written a lot
in my journal every day too.

1294
00:44:24,110 --> 00:44:26,140
Day 11 in the house.

1295
00:44:26,140 --> 00:44:27,380
Day 12.

1296
00:44:28,140 --> 00:44:29,500
Day 13.

1297
00:44:30,580 --> 00:44:31,420
Day 14.

1298
00:44:32,220 --> 00:44:37,180
(Behind-the-Scenes 16)

1299
00:44:37,180 --> 00:44:39,140
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Three, two, one.

1300
00:44:41,300 --> 00:44:41,900
No.

1301
00:44:41,900 --> 00:44:42,860
This one.

1302
00:44:42,860 --> 00:44:43,830
This one should be fine.

1303
00:44:43,830 --> 00:44:45,470
Why are the two halves different colors?

1304
00:44:45,470 --> 00:44:46,580
There's a line down the middle.

1305
00:44:46,580 --> 00:44:47,620
Cover it for a bit.

1306
00:44:48,500 --> 00:44:49,660
(Covers it)

1307
00:44:52,430 --> 00:44:53,110
This has to work.

1308
00:44:53,110 --> 00:44:53,830
It's just developing slowly.

1309
00:44:54,220 --> 00:44:55,980
(Speeds up the developing)

1310
00:44:58,670 --> 00:44:59,710
You need to warm it up.

1311
00:45:00,750 --> 00:45:01,870
This one should be okay, right?

1312
00:45:02,190 --> 00:45:02,620
It's not showing yet.

1313
00:45:02,620 --> 00:45:03,300
Still loading.

1314
00:45:03,300 --> 00:45:04,310
Give it a little longer.

1315
00:45:04,790 --> 00:45:06,230
If it looks weird, it's your camera.

1316
00:45:06,230 --> 00:45:06,790
Then it must be mine.

1317
00:45:06,790 --> 00:45:07,710
It's not my film.

1318
00:45:07,860 --> 00:45:08,300
Because...

1319
00:45:08,300 --> 00:45:09,620
No, it just hasn't developed yet.

1320
00:45:11,270 --> 00:45:12,190
(Moves closer)
It really hasn't.

1321
00:45:12,390 --> 00:45:13,310
I can see two figures now.

1322
00:45:13,310 --> 00:45:14,630
Yeah, they're showing now.

1323
00:45:14,630 --> 00:45:15,420
What's going on?

1324
00:45:15,420 --> 00:45:16,630
No way.

1325
00:45:20,620 --> 00:45:23,260
I think there might be something wrong
with the camera too.

1326
00:45:28,260 --> 00:45:29,100
(Makes eye contact)

1327
00:45:29,100 --> 00:45:29,910
(Shy)
What?

1328
00:45:30,470 --> 00:45:30,830
Looks good.

1329
00:45:30,830 --> 00:45:31,340
What are you smiling about?

1330
00:45:31,340 --> 00:45:32,150
Looks good.

1331
00:45:32,150 --> 00:45:33,180
Why'd you suddenly start smiling?

1332
00:45:33,180 --> 00:45:33,710
I wasn't.

1333
00:45:33,710 --> 00:45:34,990
I just smiled at you.

1334
00:45:36,460 --> 00:45:41,420
(Behind-the-Scenes 17)

1335
00:45:41,460 --> 00:45:41,940
(Behind-the-Scenes)

1336
00:45:41,940 --> 00:45:43,670
(Chen Hewen and Sha Yue'er city date)
Wanna try returning my smash?

1337
00:45:44,110 --> 00:45:45,700
What's a smash?

1338
00:45:45,700 --> 00:45:46,540
Here, hit one.

1339
00:45:46,540 --> 00:45:47,590
Let me feel it.

1340
00:45:48,340 --> 00:45:49,220
This?

1341
00:45:52,310 --> 00:45:53,470
I can't return that.

1342
00:45:56,550 --> 00:45:57,430
You first or me?

1343
00:45:59,020 --> 00:45:59,940
I'll go first.

1344
00:46:07,110 --> 00:46:09,510
Yeah, you need to lift it
with a backhand.

1345
00:46:12,150 --> 00:46:12,980
We're tied now.

1346
00:46:13,460 --> 00:46:14,260
(Doesn't clear the net)

1347
00:46:15,260 --> 00:46:16,170
Wow.

1348
00:46:16,790 --> 00:46:17,990
Two to one.

1349
00:46:21,460 --> 00:46:22,420
Two to two now.

1350
00:46:22,540 --> 00:46:23,540
(Smiles)

1351
00:46:23,670 --> 00:46:24,270
Okay.

1352
00:46:30,900 --> 00:46:31,820
(Clips the net and goes over)

1353
00:46:32,860 --> 00:46:33,940
Does that count?

1354
00:46:35,070 --> 00:46:35,980
It went over.

1355
00:46:36,860 --> 00:46:37,780
It didn't go over.

1356
00:46:40,510 --> 00:46:41,510
Just lift it.

1357
00:46:44,860 --> 00:46:45,860
You're really good.

1358
00:46:56,150 --> 00:46:57,430
Today was really fun.

1359
00:46:57,430 --> 00:46:58,630
Yeah, I had a great time.

1360
00:46:58,900 --> 00:47:03,860
(Behind-the-Scenes 18)

1361
00:47:03,900 --> 00:47:05,580
(Behind-the-Scenes, Cui Yihang
and Wu Siying stargazing room date)

1362
00:47:05,980 --> 00:47:07,540
(Hands over)

1363
00:47:08,150 --> 00:47:09,950
Do they know we're coming
to the stargazing room?

1364
00:47:10,150 --> 00:47:11,110
Some of them do.

1365
00:47:11,590 --> 00:47:12,710
Because Zhao Xilun went

1366
00:47:13,190 --> 00:47:13,950
to vote with his
Master Kong jasmine coin.

1367
00:47:15,190 --> 00:47:16,150
He wanted to vote
for the stargazing room?

1368
00:47:16,150 --> 00:47:16,590
Yeah.

1369
00:47:16,590 --> 00:47:18,270
After voting, he'd naturally

1370
00:47:18,270 --> 00:47:19,830
grab the key and come check.

1371
00:47:20,870 --> 00:47:21,910
(Joking)
I locked it right away.

1372
00:47:23,390 --> 00:47:24,190
He went to the bathroom.

1373
00:47:25,630 --> 00:47:27,380
He didn't expect me
to come out for a walk.

1374
00:47:27,380 --> 00:47:29,150
I thought Zhao Xilun seemed
a little awkward earlier.

1375
00:47:31,700 --> 00:47:34,110
Are tulips out of season?

1376
00:47:34,950 --> 00:47:35,870
Why?

1377
00:47:35,990 --> 00:47:36,750
Because...

1378
00:47:36,750 --> 00:47:37,750
(Avoids eye contact)
I couldn't find any.

1379
00:47:39,430 --> 00:47:40,470
What season do they bloom?

1380
00:47:40,830 --> 00:47:42,470
Probably April.

1381
00:47:43,910 --> 00:47:45,070
Back in April,

1382
00:47:45,430 --> 00:47:48,030
there were tons of tulips outside

1383
00:47:48,310 --> 00:47:48,830
my office.

1384
00:47:49,350 --> 00:47:50,510
They came in all kinds of colors.

1385
00:47:50,710 --> 00:47:52,070
Actually, the flowers
from your date that day

1386
00:47:52,070 --> 00:47:53,270
are in my room.

1387
00:47:53,510 --> 00:47:54,470
Are they doing okay?

1388
00:47:54,470 --> 00:47:55,110
They're doing great.

1389
00:47:55,190 --> 00:47:55,950
They're great every day.

1390
00:47:55,950 --> 00:47:57,950
They get a little better every day.

1391
00:47:57,950 --> 00:47:59,980
(Better every day)

1392
00:48:09,180 --> 00:48:14,140
(Behind-the-Scenes 19)

1393
00:48:14,390 --> 00:48:19,550
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Put my medicine in my bag.

1394
00:48:19,550 --> 00:48:20,340
Okay.

1395
00:48:20,780 --> 00:48:22,100
Such a happy day.

1396
00:48:23,390 --> 00:48:24,950
Today felt so short.

1397
00:48:26,260 --> 00:48:27,140
It's...

1398
00:48:27,470 --> 00:48:28,750
We still have plenty of days.

1399
00:48:28,750 --> 00:48:30,190
It's already nighttime.

1400
00:48:30,430 --> 00:48:33,190
We still have plenty of days.

1401
00:48:35,190 --> 00:48:36,230
What's that tasty-looking thing?

1402
00:48:36,230 --> 00:48:37,030
Let me see.

1403
00:48:39,510 --> 00:48:40,780
Crawfish?

1404
00:48:40,780 --> 00:48:41,980
We drove past it.

1405
00:48:42,550 --> 00:48:43,670
Then I'll pull over.

1406
00:48:47,910 --> 00:48:48,870
Crispy grilled sausage.

1407
00:48:48,870 --> 00:48:51,150
I'll pull over for crispy sausage too.

1408
00:48:52,470 --> 00:48:53,350
I'm not hungry.

1409
00:48:53,590 --> 00:48:54,390
I can't be hungry.

1410
00:48:54,630 --> 00:48:55,750
I refuse to be hungry.

1411
00:49:02,460 --> 00:49:03,980
(Notices)

1412
00:49:04,700 --> 00:49:05,820
Thanks for driving.

1413
00:49:05,820 --> 00:49:07,180
It's really fine.

1414
00:49:07,180 --> 00:49:08,060
Thanks.

